Package: LJM
Title: Local Joint Models for Dynamic Survival Prediction
Version: 1.0.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jinwoo", "Cho", email = "jinoojwcho@cmu.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Kehui", "Chen", role = "aut"))
Description: Dynamic prediction of survival outcomes from multiple noisy
    longitudinal biomarkers using the local joint model (LJM). Around a
    landmark time, each biomarker trajectory is summarised by a kernel-weighted
    local linear approximation, i.e. its recent level (intercept) and change
    (slope), and a transformation survival model relates these summaries to the
    conditional risk. Estimation uses a fast EM algorithm with one-dimensional
    adaptive quadrature, so its cost does not grow exponentially with the
    number of biomarkers. The package supports time-varying association
    functions via B-splines and provides dynamic prediction with
    time-dependent AUC and prediction-error evaluation. See Cho and Chen
    (2026) for methodological details.
